# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Data — never commit. See README for how to obtain it.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/sickle_data/
*.zip
*.npz
*.tif
*.pth
*.pth.tar

# Reference implementation is cloned, not vendored (see README)
/reference_impl/

# Scratch
/outputs/
*.log

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Results ARE tracked, deliberately.
#
# Every headline claim in docs/ is backed by a file under results/ or
# artifacts/. A run manifest that records a commit hash is worthless if the
# evidence that hash is meant to pin is not in the tree. These are all small
# (JSON/CSV/PNG, ~1.2 MB total), so they are committed rather than ignored:
#
#   results/gate/           12 cells x one JSON — the reproduction gate
#   results/plot_level/     Plot-Macro IoU + bootstrap CI per cell
#   results/previews/       human-viewable imagery
#   artifacts/subsets/      the 30 nested plot manifests the sweep uses
#   results/_discarded_unknown_batchsize/
#                           the contaminated first sweep, kept so the process
#                           failure in docs/REPRODUCTION_GATE.md 4a stays
#                           auditable. Not used for anything.
#
# Large training outputs (checkpoints, 155-run logs) are excluded by the
# *.pth.tar rule above and by /outputs/.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# OS
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Training outputs: checkpoints are large and logs are per-run scratch.
# best.json / manifest.json / trainlog.json ARE tracked (see below) because
# they are the evidence; the weights are not.
/outputs/logs/
/outputs/**/checkpoint_*.pth.tar
